@startuml
title Apply Order Collaboration Diagram
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false

actor Applicant as A
actor Publisher as P
rectangle Client as C
rectangle OrderController as OC
rectangle OrderServiceImpl as OS
database MySQL as DB

A --> C : 1 browseOrder()
C --> OC : 2 apply(orderId)
OC --> OS : 3 applyOrder(request)
OS --> DB : 4 insertApplication()
DB --> OS : 5 applyId
OS --> OC : 6 result
OC --> C : 7 applySuccess

P --> C : 8 openApplicationList()
C --> OC : 9 getApplications()
OC --> OS : 10 loadApplications()
OS --> DB : 11 selectApplications()
DB --> OS : 12 applications
OS --> OC : 13 applications
OC --> C : 14 showList

P --> C : 15 approve()
C --> OC : 16 auditApply(applyId)
OC --> OS : 17 updateStatus(APPROVED)
OS --> DB : 18 updateApplication()
DB --> OS : 19 ok
OS --> OC : 20 approved
OC --> C : 21 notifySuccess

note bottom of OS
  Collaboration diagrams emphasize
  cooperating objects and numbered messages.
end note

@enduml
